            <title>[LU-20990] sanity test_43A: lfs mkdir dirstripe error: Input/output error</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20990</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_43A's test_mkdir helper hit:&lt;br/&gt;
lfs mkdir: dirstripe error on '/mnt/lustre/d43A.sanity': Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
lfs mkdir: cannot create dir '/mnt/lustre/d43A.sanity': Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/ea5283e1-15ef-40f4-b0bf-2282b2eaf0d2" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/ea5283e1-15ef-40f4-b0bf-2282b2eaf0d2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rare and ambient: 2 of 17188 sanity runs in the last 30 days (fail_rate&lt;br/&gt;
0.0001). The same error hit an unrelated change (59419, patchset 2) on&lt;br/&gt;
2026-10-07, and a retest of that session failed again the same way, so&lt;br/&gt;
this is not tied to change 69320. Patch 69320 only reserves an&lt;br/&gt;
OBD_CONNECT2 flag and adds wire-constant checks; it touches none of the&lt;br/&gt;
striped mkdir path. No open LU ticket names sanity test_43A with this&lt;br/&gt;
error; similar dirstripe-create EIO failures exist under &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16289" title="replay-single test_70d: dirstripe error on '/mnt/lustre/d70d.replay-single/test': Input/output error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16289"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16289&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16855" title="sanity-scrub test_4c: lfs mkdir: dirstripe error on '/mnt/lustre/d4c.sanity-scrub/mds4': Input/output error" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16855"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16855&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18142" title="sanity-flr test_70: mkdir -i 2 -c2 -H crush /mnt/lustre/d70.sanity-flr failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18142"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18142&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20604" title="sanity test_24C: create striped dir failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20604"&gt;LU-20604&lt;/a&gt;, but each is a different test or a&lt;br/&gt;
different underlying error (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20604" title="sanity test_24C: create striped dir failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20604"&gt;LU-20604&lt;/a&gt;'s is 'Required key not&lt;br/&gt;
available').&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69320-ps13-720e51c94e86 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69320" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69320&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
